{#- A portrait entry (.person, About and Team; content file 5.12, 5.13): one person from
    src/site/_data/team.json, its id the person's slug (3.2), the name as an h3 with any credentials
    after it, the role in the label voice, and, when asked, the portrait and the bio. The portrait is
    the company's own (person-<slug>, small, never upscaled) and its alt is the person's name; a bio
    paragraph over 60 words is split at a sentence (R1, the paragraphs filter). Import it with context:
    {% from "person.njk" import person with context %}; person(p, { photo: true, bio: true }); { credentials: false } leaves the credentials out (Team, whose
    founders' line in 5.13 is name and role). -#}
{%- from "picture.njk" import picture with context -%}
{%- macro person(p, opts) -%}
<li class="person{% if opts.photo %} has-photo{% endif %}" id="{{ p.slug }}">
  {%- if opts.photo %}
  {{ picture("person-" + p.slug, p.name, "(min-width: 64rem) 10rem, (min-width: 30rem) 8rem, 6.5rem", { class: "person-photo" }) }}
  {%- endif %}
  <div class="person-head">
    <h3 class="person-name">{{ p.name }}{% if p.credentials and opts.credentials !== false %} <span class="person-credentials">{{ p.credentials }}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
    {%- if p.role %}
    <p class="label person-role">{{ p.role }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- if opts.bio and p.bio %}
  <div class="person-bio">
    {%- for para in p.bio | paragraphs %}
    <p>{{ para }}</p>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</li>
{%- endmacro -%}
